00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:17.970
Cloud computing
platforms are built

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.490
on some of the most exciting,
sophisticated technology

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.655
in the world.

00:00:21.655 --> 00:00:23.280
But what makes the
Cloud truly valuable

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.388
is the amazing software that
you build and run on it.

00:00:26.388 --> 00:00:27.930
Let's take a look
at how Google Cloud

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:31.620
Platform helps you develop,
deploy, and debug in the Cloud.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.350
GCP leverages Google's
deep expertise

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.300
in building world-class
software to bring you

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.340
an amazing development
environment.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.470
As a developer, you
need actionable insights

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.960
throughout the entire
software lifecycle and tools

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:45.310
to integrate from
each phase to the next

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:47.130
so you can continuously
iterate and improve

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.690
on your applications.

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.220
Let's start with the code.

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:51.870
Google's Cloud
Source Repositories

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:55.170
is enterprise-grade Git
hosting for private repos.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:57.800
It's architected to scale
up to massive code bases

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.240
and provides extremely
high availability.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.220
And it provides
security intelligence

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:04.530
to prevent sensitive
data, like access keys,

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.170
from ever landing in your repo.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.210
CSR also comes with code search.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.710
You can search
across multiple repos

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.588
at once, using advanced syntax
like regular expressions.

00:01:14.588 --> 00:01:16.380
Code search is built
on the same technology

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.910
as Google's famous
search engine,

00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:20.010
so it truly understands code.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.380
Entities like classes,
functions, and fields

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.690
are indexed and displayed
as real-time suggestions

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.710
for fast navigation.

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:30.030
Next, deploying applications--
Cloud Source Repositories

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.820
is pre-integrated with
Cloud Build, Google Cloud's

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:35.310
fully-managed CI/CD platform.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.340
Use Cloud Build to compile,
test, package, and deploy

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.800
your code to any
Google Cloud Runtime,

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.960
including Compute Engine,
Kubernetes Engine,

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.630
and Cloud Run.

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:49.080
But maybe not everything
should get deployed.

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:52.050
How can you be sure that
what you're running is safe?

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.670
Google's got your
back with services

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.680
that actively detect
software vulnerabilities

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.140
in every artifact you store
in your private Container

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.370
Registry.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.870
When you pair
vulnerability scanning

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.455
with binary authorization
for Kubernetes Engine,

00:02:03.455 --> 00:02:04.830
you'll have a
powerful gatekeeper

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:06.693
protecting your infrastructure.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.110
Only artifacts that have been
given a clean bill of health

00:02:09.110 --> 00:02:11.440
will have permission
to run on your cluster.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.140
Finally, debugging
a running system--

00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:16.410
Cloud Source Repositories
works with Stackdriver

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.810
to unlock your
developer superpowers.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:21.600
Are you trying to wrangle
a hard-to-reproduce bug?

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.040
With the Stackdriver
Debugger, you

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.830
can attach break points at
specific points in your code

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:28.500
or capture a complete
snapshot of application state

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:30.390
to find that needle
in the haystack.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.700
Amazingly, all of this
happens without any need

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.800
to revise or redeploy
your code and

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:36.930
with no appreciable
performance impact.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:40.230
Use these diagnostic tools
on the fly, in real time,

00:02:40.230 --> 00:02:42.580
for production workloads.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.180
This was just a taste of the
powerful developer experience

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.842
on Google Cloud Platform.

